n: create\n        note: DiffTest struct, RunDiffTest function, comparison and reporting logic\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Define DiffTest struct with fields for test name, binary paths (Go and reference), command-line arguments, stdin input, environment variables, and expected exit code per prd004-testutils\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement RunDiffTest that executes both binaries with identical stdin, arguments, and environment, then compares stdout, stderr, and exit code byte-for-byte\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Report divergence with the triggering input, expected output (reference binary), and actual output (Go binary) as a structured error\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Support normalization hooks (func(string) string) applied to stdout/stderr before comparison, for known acceptable differences such as timestamps\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Primary file is difftest.go per P7 naming convention -- the primary exported type is DiffTest\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Package is pkg/testutils/ per ARCHITECTURE.yaml component definition\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Use os/exec to run both binaries; do not import pkg/sys (testutils is lower-level infrastructure)\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"DiffTest struct is defined with all fields specified in the PRD\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"RunDiffTest executes both binaries and returns nil when outputs match\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"RunDiffTest returns a descriptive error when stdout, stderr, or exit code diverge\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Normalization hooks are applied before comparison when provided\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Code compiles with go build ./pkg/testutils/\"\n\nNow I'm second-guessing the PRD numbering scheme. Looking at the existing pattern—prd002-sys, prd003-format, prd011-magefiles—it's not immediately clear where testutils fits. It could be prd001